  {
   "id": "note-full",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1500,
   "y": 84,
   "width": 520,
   "height": 190,
   "text": "**Full layers** (every 6th): head 512 instead of 256, so q / o are 2× wider and K/V cache 2,048 values per token vs 1,024. **p-RoPE**: only the first 128 of 512 dims rotate (θ 1,000,000); the rest carry no position. The last layer is always full."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-ffn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1150,
   "y": 1088,
   "width": 480,
   "height": 150,
   "text": "**One sliding layer** = 93.1M: FFN 78.6M (84%), attention 13.1M, per-layer-input block 1.3M. A full layer = 106.2M."
  }
